# Agent tooling. Same category as .idea and .vscode above: local scratch
# rather than anything the project needs to build or run.
#
# worktrees/ in particular held a FULL SECOND CHECKOUT of this repo, and
# was covered only by .git/info/exclude -- which is per-clone and does not
# travel, so the protection existed on exactly one machine. A `git add -A`
# anywhere else would have committed a duplicate of the entire tree.
#
# CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT in here: it lives at the repo root and is
# committed, because the house rules are the project's, not the tool's.
.claude/
